KEPT, one character. src/game/world/gauntworld.c, the trailing loop of the world-name entry display:
    while (i < 6) {
        DrawTextKeepScale(lbl_80346DB4, (u16)x - 4, 340, 7, white,
                          (u8*)"");
becomes (u8*)"_". EVIDENCE, three independent readings of the same fact: (1) `fnasm game/world/gauntworld fn_8005A868 0x340:0x380` shows the target's loop body ending `@0x364 li r7,0 R_PPC_EMB_SDA21 lbl_80346DB8` / `@0x368 bl DrawTextKeepScale`, i.e. the 6th argument is the address of lbl_80346DB8; (2) build/GUNE5D/asm/auto_11_80345D70_sdata2.s:3607-3609 declares `.obj lbl_80346DB8, global / .string "_" / .endobj`, and the next object starts at 0x80346DBA, so the datum is exactly two bytes '_' NUL; (3) `fndiff game/world/gauntworld fn_8005A868 --clean` reported it verbatim before the edit: `POOL-DEFECT ... pool@0x364 target lbl_80346DB8 = +0x0 '_.'   ours @3955 = +0x0 '.'   VALUES DIFFER (first at +0x0)`. BEHAVIOUR: retail draws an underscore in each unfilled slot of the six-character world-name entry field (the classic name-entry placeholder); our reconstruction drew an empty string, so the unfilled slots rendered as nothing. The x advance, colour, font and scale were already correct, so the defect was exactly the glyph.
